# The app's environment for the Scenarios (tools/verify/scenarios): one
# NAME=value per line, set for the Scenario run's next build and next start, and
# for its Playwright runs, so a Scenario reads the same values (never for smoke
# or playtest). Blank lines and # comments are ignored; NAME is capitals, digits
# and _, not starting with a digit, and none of the driver's own (NX_*,
# FACTORY_*). The value is the rest of the line, as written. In it the driver puts:
#   {fixtures}  its fixture server, http://127.0.0.1:<port>, at the fixed port
#               FACTORY_SCENARIO_FIXTURE_PORT (local.env): what the app fetches
#               there, a Scenario serves (the driver's header says how)
#   {state}     a folder of the run's own, emptied before each Scenario file
# For example, an app that reads a feed and keeps a cache:
#   FEED_URL={fixtures}/feed.ics
#   CACHE_PATH={state}/cache.sqlite
# None by default: the app runs as its own config says.

# The calendar feed from the fixture server, a cache of the run's own, and
# the revalidation route (src/app/api/revalidate/route.ts) that lets a Scenario
# make the pages read them again.
CALENDAR_FEED_URL={fixtures}/calendar.ics
EVENTS_CACHE_PATH={state}/events.sqlite
ON_DEMAND_REVALIDATION=1
